        "original_id": "69475a7e-dd1f-5424-9c5b-80d559590d8c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Little Missouri River, Devils Tower, Three V Crossing, Missouri River, Belle Fourche River\n- Topics: river geography, landforms, locations in Wyoming, Montana, South Dakota, and North Dakota\n\nFacts:\n- The Little Missouri River is a 560-mile (901 km) tributary of the Missouri River in the northern Great Plains of the United States.\n- The Little Missouri River rises in northeastern Wyoming in western Crook County about 15 miles (24 km) west of Devils Tower.\n- The Little Missouri River flows northeast across a corner of southeastern Montana and into South Dakota.\n- Devils Tower, also called Bear Lodge Butte, is a laccolithic butte of igneous rock in the Bear Lodge Mountains of the Black Hills near Hulett and Sundance in Crook County, northeastern Wyoming, above the Belle Fourche River.\n- Devils Tower rises 1,267 feet (386 m) above the Belle Fourche River and stands 867 feet (265 m) from summit to base.\n- Three V Crossing is on the Little Missouri River 19.1 miles north-northeast of Marmarth, North Dakota.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "98d636f5-40b1-5162-ab18-1451c032b681",
        "text": "Page: Little Missouri River (North Dakota). Sentence: The Little Missouri River is a tributary of the Missouri River, 560 miles (901 km) long, in the northern Great Plains of the United States.\nPage: Little Missouri River (North Dakota). Sentence: Rising in northeastern Wyoming, in western Crook County about 15 miles (24 km) west of Devils Tower, it flows northeastward, across a corner of southeastern Montana, and into South Dakota.\nPage: Devils Tower. Sentence: Devils Tower (also Bear Lodge Butte) is a laccolithic butte composed of igneous rock in the Bear Lodge Mountains (part of the Black Hills) near Hulett and Sundance in Crook County, northeastern Wyoming, above the Belle Fourche River.\nPage: Devils Tower. Sentence: It rises dramatically 1,267 feet (386 m) above the Belle Fourche River, standing 867 feet (265 m) from summit to base.\nPage: Three V Crossing, North Dakota. Sentence: Three V Crossing is located on the Little Missouri River 19.1 mi north-northeast of Marmarth.",
